# Whale Girl — Spec Compliance

- The specs are the constitution: specs/{mission,tech-stack,roadmap}.md.
  Behavior changes start there, never in code first.
- Before every write to disk, an ask-user-question round grouped on requirements
  (scope/decisions/context), plan (task groups), and validation (success criteria)
  must be answered by the user.
- Never add dependencies outside specs/tech-stack.md. Never skip or
  reorder roadmap items without owner approval.
- Feature specs live in specs/features/YYYY-MM-DD-<item>/ with
  requirements.md, plan.md, validation.md; validation.md must end with a "Handoff to
  dependant milestones" list when work is deferred.
- Verification is two-sided: the agent's automatic half (probes, smoke checks,
  node --check) AND the owner's manual half (browser ?debug=1, OBS).
- Agents never git commit / git push; leave changes uncommitted for owner review.
- Roadmap history: tick the roadmap item and archive full detail in
  specs/history_roadmap.md at the close.
